  "description": "Closes the bridge from van der Veen's constant E to this corpus's c_sigma, for the whole b=1 Whitehead-chain family. Derives c_sigma = 2^{1/2-n}(n^2+m^2)^{-1/4} (n = c+d, m = 4a-c+d) from his Lemmas 1-4, correcting three slips in the published proof, and verifies it against Q_N computed directly from Lemma 1 on 20 chains. RETRACTS this probe's earlier orthant-probability closed form, which was downstream of an unchecked premise. Implies |tau_DG| = 2^{2n-2} sqrt(n^2+m^2), confirmed to 18 digits at L5a1, L6a4 and - pre-registered - L8n5, L10n100, L10n103. Makes the constant k = 2^{-1/2} derived rather than calibrated on the link side. Moduli only; the phase of E is not checked. Nothing fitted.",
  "auditOnly": "docs/audits/2026-08-08-vdv-constant-closed-form-and-the-open-bridge.md",
  "data": {
    "source": {
      "paper": "van der Veen, Proof of the volume conjecture for Whitehead chains, Algebr. Geom. Topol. 8 (2008) 603-624",
      "arxiv": "math/0611181",
      "local": "uploads/0611181v2.pdf",
      "what_he_proves": "the volume conjecture for the family, D = 3 pi for b = 1",
      "what_he_leaves": "E, as a (c+d+1)-dim Gaussian integral; he shows only that it is nonzero, which is all his theorem needs",
      "sequel_status": "no sequel exists; his later work moves to spin networks, and no other author has published this constant for a multi-cusped link in this setting"
    },
    "retraction": {
      "what_was_claimed": "Step 6 reduces E to a Gaussian-against-erfc^n integral, an (n+1)-dim orthant probability, with elementary closed forms arctan(sqrt A)/(pi sqrt(A/2)) at n=1 and an arcsin form at n=2",
      "why_it_was_wrong": "the erfc factors come from folding the Step-4 Gaussian onto an orthant, which is an artifact of Lemma 2a being stated in the DISTANCES |n'|,|k'| rather than the signed offsets its own Taylor expansion supplies",
      "why_the_old_checks_missed_it": "both the 1e-25 quadrature check and the independent Step-5 cross-check were downstream of that integrand; they tested the reduction, never the premise. Nothing was compared against J_N itself, which is the only check that could have caught it",
