        "printed": "exp(-(pi/N)(n'^2 + 2 n' k' + 2 k'^2)), n',k' distances",
        "correct": "the same form in the SIGNED offsets n - floor(N/2), k - floor(N/4)",
        "signed_form_wins_on_every_sample": true,
        "consequence": "the Step-4 integral is over R^(n+1), so it is elementary for every n, not only n <= 2"
      },
      "step3_coefficient_A": {
